  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Every time I put the oven on it runs for a few minutes and then the trip switch goes and half the house loses power. Reset it 3 times tonight. Hotpoint built-in, about 9 years old. What could cause this?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nPlease don't keep resetting the trip. Leave the appliance unplugged and have it checked by a qualified electrician or appliance engineer before using it again. This symptom indicates a significant electrical fault, likely a short circuit or earth leakage within the oven’s heating elements or wiring. Because it causes your main RCD to trip and affects half the house, you should stop using the appliance immediately. From what you have checked, this needs an appliance engineer to look at it: the next steps are beyond the checks that are safe to do yourself."
  }
